A||N||1||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||Duke Intake Manifold Restrictor Plate Under TBI, WHY? What if it went "bye-bye"?||||5||
Z||000000||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||01-24-2001||01:35 AM||||I think theogre said in a previous post that the little baffle plate placed under the TBI in the 2.5L intake manifold is there to improve flow to cylinders 1 and 4.<P>I have looked at it really hard, and I am "baffled" as to how it improves flow to any of the cylinders.  It seems like an intake baffle to me.  <P>I want to take it out because it looks like a stupid after-thought made to increase fuel economy, improve emmisions, and make the car quieter.  These add-ons may be great for people who bought cadillacs in the 80s, but my fiero could get a little louder and it would not bother me.  It passes smog with near zero readings, so there seems to be room for a 10 fold increase in emissions with no consequence.  I doubt the little intake restrictor does anything to help the car run better.  <P>What if I just take the stupid thing out of my intake manifold?  TheOgre, how could it be a mistake??????||||reg||5
Z||000001||Tom Philips||01-24-2001||07:34 AM||||the restrictor plate is used for a more even air fuel distribution between cylinders. The plate was not used very long and if you take it nothing will happen except some cylinders run rich and some lean||||reg||1
